# MPTC constraint with undeclared TypeVar — should produce type error
# Tests that bind: validation works for MPTC constraints
#
# NOTE: This test currently cannot use $Add because Add is not registered in class_env
# (it only exists as a constraint in the + builtin's TypeScheme). MPTC syntax parsing
# is implemented, but full MPTC validation requires the class to be in class_env.
# This test will need to be updated when Add class registration is added.

---
--- stage: type
or: [fn [a b] [kind: "union" members: [a b]]]
---

# For now, test that 'each' keyword works in constraints
multi-constrained: [fn@[bind: [a] constraint: [a: [each Comparable Showable]] return: a]
  [x@a] x]

[multi-constrained 42]
---
EVAL
42
---
TYPE
Int
---
TYPECHECK-ONLY
